{#- NX-OS VXLAN GPO (security groups): class-maps, policy-maps and group definitions.

    `group_policy` (transforms/helpers/group_policy.py vxlan_gpo_device_view) is
    set only on a VTEP of a reference fabric; every block here is guarded by it,
    so a device without one renders exactly as before. The contracts and
    `security enforce` live in the tenant `vrf context` (cisco_nxos_vxlan_vrf.j2).
    Included before the VXLAN block, after the VLANs (a `match vlan` needs its
    VLAN). Evidence per line: D documented (NX-OS 10.6(x) VXLAN guide, GPO
    chapter); every I/U line says documented-not-lab-verified.
    Never rendered: `system security-group mac-segmentation` (it disables the
    IP-based segmentation), intra-group isolation, TCAM vacl, PVLAN. -#}
{%- if group_policy and (group_policy.class_maps or group_policy.groups) %}
!
! Group policy (VXLAN GPO): one class-map and policy-map per distinct entry set, then the security groups
{%- for class_map in group_policy.class_maps %}
! {{ class_map.name }}: {{ class_map.entries }}
{%- for note in class_map.notes %}
! documented-not-lab-verified: {{ note }}
{%- endfor %}
class-map type security match-any {{ class_map.name }}
{%- for line in class_map.lines %}
  {{ line }}
{%- endfor %}
policy-map type security {{ class_map.name }}
  class {{ class_map.name }}
    permit
{%- endfor %}
!
! Security groups: the VLAN selector is this device's own VLAN of the segment; a group without one is
! classified on the VTEPs that carry its segment (the group ID travels in the VXLAN header)
! documented-not-lab-verified: the guide gives no range for the group ids and no rules for the group names (a tag name is rewritten to [A-Za-z0-9_-])
{%- for group in group_policy.groups %}
{%- for note in group.notes %}
! {{ note }}
{%- endfor %}
security-group {{ group.id }} name {{ group.name }}
{%- if group.vlan_id %}
  match vlan {{ group.vlan_id }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
!
{%- endif -%}
